<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pashtuns</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pathans, Pakhtuns, Pukhtuns</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pashtuns are an Iranian-speaking people of southern and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, speaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pashto">Pashto</a> and organised in many tribes and clans. Their customary code, Pashtunwali, stresses honour, hospitality and the tribal council, or jirga. Pashtun dynasties such as the Hotaks and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durrani-empire">Durranis</a> founded the modern Afghan state in the 18th century.</p></div>
